{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And HaShem Elohim commanded concerning the human.</b> He did not test him for His own sake, for everything that was and would be was revealed before Him; rather, to satisfy the minds of the angels of mercy, who were seeking mercy for him excessively — He showed them that he would not withstand the test. And our Sages derived from here seven commandments for the children of Noah." "<b>Vayetzav.</b> These are laws (דינין). And so it says: ״כי ידעתיו למען אשר יצוה״ etc." "<b>YHWH.</b> This is the glory of the Holy One, blessed be He. And so it says: ״ונקב שם ה׳ מות יומת.״" "<b>Elohim.</b> This is idolatry. And so it says: ״לא יהיה לך אלהים אחרים.״" "<b>Concerning the human.</b> This is the shedding of blood. And so it says: ״שופך דם האדם.״" "<b>Saying.</b> This is the prohibition of forbidden relations, and so it says: לאמר הן ישלח איש את אשתו." "<b>From every tree of the garden.</b> This is robbery." "<b>You shall surely eat.</b> This is a limb from a living animal. Abraham came and added circumcision. Jacob came and added the sinew of the thigh. Judah came and added the commandment of levirate marriage. Israel came and added upon them Sabbath and honoring father and mother." "<b>Upon the human.</b> Upon him and upon his seed after him — therefore it does not write את האדם." "<b>[Upon the human.</b> Upon all the limbs of the human.]" "<b>Of every tree of the garden you may freely eat.</b> And if you ask: if so, the defender has an opening to argue that he ate from the tree of life. And if so, how was death decreed upon him afterward, when he ate from the tree of knowledge? One may answer that he did not eat from the tree of life, for he did not remain in the Garden of Eden but three hours. And if you should say he did eat from it — perhaps the tree of knowledge is a deadly poison for one who has eaten from the tree of life, and the tree of life is a deadly poison for one who has eaten from the tree of knowledge. Therefore, after he ate from the tree of knowledge, HaKadosh Baruch Hu said: 'the man has become like one of us, to know good and evil, and now, lest he stretch out his hand and take also from the tree of life a second time and eat and live forever' — and the creatures would be likely to stray after him. But since he did not eat from the tree of life after the tree of knowledge, he will surely die. Another interpretation: <b>of every tree of the garden you may freely eat</b> — it does not refer to the tree of life, for it needs no warning. For what is written, 'the tree of life in the midst of the garden,' means in the middle of the garden, and proof for this is that its Targum is 'in the middle of the garden.' And the tree of knowledge surrounded it entirely, around all its sides, so that both of them were in the middle of the garden; and as long as he does not pass through and take from the tree of knowledge, the tree of life is guarded within it. Therefore he was warned only about the tree of knowledge, and when he transgressed and ate from it, then HaKadosh Baruch Hu said: 'the man has become like one of us,' etc. Another interpretation: man was permitted to eat of every tree of the garden except the tree of knowledge, as it is written <b>but of the tree of knowledge you shall not eat of it</b> — for as long as you do not eat of it, you will have no awareness and inclination to distinguish between good and evil, and I judge you only as inadvertent, and you are not a sinner, and there is no concern if you live forever, since you will not sin. But if you taste of it, I judge you as intentional and decree death upon you, lest you be a living sinner forever. Another interpretation: the reason man was not warned about the tree of life is because he was destined to transgress a commandment, and it is better that he eat from the tree of knowledge than from the tree of life."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:45.191597230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}